HASHI MASAKAZU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HOSOKAWA CHISHIO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>IKEDA HIDETSUGU</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KAWAMURA HISAYUKI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KOGA HIDETOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>ARAI, HIROMASA</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>FUNEHASHI, MASAKAZU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HOSOKAWA, CHISHIO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>IKEDA, HIDETSUGU</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KAWAMURA, HISAYUKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KOGA, HIDETOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A material for organic electroluminescent elements having a high luminescent efficiency, a long life, and high heat resistance; and a process for producing the material. The material is represented by gereral formula (1). In the formula, A represents optionally substituted C22-60 arylene; X&lt;1&gt; to X&lt;4&gt; each represents optionally substituted C6-30 arylene; Y&lt;1&gt; to Y&lt;4&gt; each represents an organic group represented by general formula (2); and a to d each is 0 to 2. In the formula, R&lt;1&gt; to R&lt;4&gt; each represents hydrogen, optionally substituted alkyl or aryl, or cyano, provided that R&lt;3&gt; may be bonded to R&lt;4&gt; to form a triple bond; Z represents optionally substituted aryl; and n is 0 or 1.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une substance destinée à être utilisée dans des éléments électroluminescents organiques présentant une luminescence élevée, une durée de vie prolongée, et une résistance à la chaleur satisfaisante. Cette substance est représentée par la formule générale (1). Dans cette formule, A représente arylène C22-60 éventuellement substitué; X&lt;1&gt; à X&lt;4&gt; désignent chacun arylène C6-30 éventuellement substitué; Y&lt;1&gt; à Y&lt;4&gt; symbolisent chacun un groupe organique représenté par la formule générale (2); et a à d varient chacun entre 0 et 2. Dans cette formule, R&lt;1&gt; à R&lt;4&gt; représentent chacun hydrogène, alkyle ou aryle éventuellement substitué, ou cyano, à condition que R&lt;3&gt; puisse être lié à R&lt;4&gt; pour former une triple liaison; Z symbolise aryle éventuellement substitué; et n se situe entre 0 et 1.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>